Key Behavioral Changes:
User Experience: 
You can customize the font size of the Fluent graphical user interface (GUI), allowing you to adjust it for your operating system, screen resolution, and personal preference. 
Graphics, Reporting, and Postprocessing: 
Enhanced interactive plots are the new default plotting framework for 2D plots. 
Solution animations are saved in the same directory as the case file. This relative path is indicated by a dot (.). 
Plotting: 
The 'Automatic Solution Initialization and Case Modification' dialog box is replaced by a more robust interface, including a new 'Case Modification Manager' dialog box, an associated 'Auto Initialization Method' dialog box, and a 'Modify Case' dialog box. 
Reacting Flows: 
[Species and composition PDF transport models] - The Inlet Diffusion option is no longer available in the Species Model dialog box because it is not considered a physically plausible boundary condition. 
Solver-Numerics: 
For transient flows, the default convergence criterion for locally scaled residuals is increased from 10-5 to 10-4. 
Solver-Meshing: 
The Unified Remeshing method is now used by default. This simplifies Dynamic Mesh setup and generally provides improved robustness, especially in parallel. 
Refer to the Ansys, Inc. Release Notes for a full listing of the new features included in Ansys Fluent 2022 R2. 
